{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "An order of the ancient Knights Radiant, many of whom disliked the name for sounding like \"Voidbringers\" and preferred to be called Releasers.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "36" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "An order of the Knights Radiant, bonded to ashspren, whose Surges of Division and Abrasion let them burn, degrade and slicken.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Dustbringers use the Surges of Division and Abrasion, and form Nahel bonds with ashspren.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The ancient Radiants",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "36" },
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Many Dustbringers objected to their order's name for sounding like \"Voidbringers\" and asked to be called Releasers.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "36" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "They claimed to be misjudged because of the dreadful nature of their power.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "36" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "During the final battle of the Last Desolation, the Dustbringers' powers left burning corpses and growth and smouldering rock.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "In one of Dalinar's visions, a Dustbringer and her squires hunt a spren corrupted by Sja-anat, then fight a thunderclast.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The True Desolation",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "27" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "3" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "3" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "17" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Malata, a Dustbringer, arrives at Urithiru with Taravangian. She says her spren Spark suggested they come.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "27" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Spark is the first ashspren known to bond someone since the Recreance. Many of her friends died in the Recreance, and she says she wants only revenge and to break things.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "3" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "By 1174 there are other Dustbringers. Lopen asks the new Dustbringer Ral-na not to talk with them, for political reasons, and Jasnah suspects the order of rebellion.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "3" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "17" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Ideals of the Dustbringers",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Ideals, also called the Immortal Words, are the rules Radiants live by. The First Ideal is shared by every order and serves as the motto of the Knights Radiant; the other four are each order's own.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The First Ideal",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Dustbringers share the First Ideal with every other order. It is broadly read as valuing life, strength and service, and the way a goal is reached.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
            }
          ],
          "words": [
            {
              "text": "Life before death, strength before weakness, journey before destination.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }],
              "spokenBy": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Abilities",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Dustbringers use the Surges of Division and Abrasion.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Like most Radiants, Dustbringers have squires; one in Dalinar's visions has about a dozen.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Many Dustbringer tactics rely on intimidation.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "90" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Division",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Division lets them make things burn, degrade or turn to dust, with fine control: Malata engraves a table with it. It also works on living flesh.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Abrasion",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                    { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "90" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Abrasion changes the friction between two surfaces. In one of Dalinar's visions, a Dustbringer glides across the water of the Purelake.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "They can lower the friction between their bodies and other surfaces to move with ease, or make objects slippery to anyone but themselves.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Abrasion can also raise the friction between two objects.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" },
                    { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "90" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
